FIXED: shared/system.css, shared/kinetic.js
  — Respect system preferences (reduced motion) and the site's own Effects switch
  — The name's colour drift and pencil wobble now stop when Effects is switched off or reduced motion is chosen mid-visit (they used to keep going until the page was reloaded)
FIXED: index-src.html (seek bars of the mini and full-screen players)
  — Screen reader announcements: a control must state its current value
  — The seek slider no longer reads "Nothing playing" during a song; it now reports "1:00 of 2:57" on load, play, pause, jump and every 15 s (not while focused, to avoid talking over the music)
FIXED: index-src.html (player cover images)
  — Meaningful contextual text: alt text must describe the image; decorative images get alt=""
  — The full-screen player's cover is now described as "Album cover: <album name>" instead of the placeholder "Now playing"; the mini player's cover (inside an already-named button) is marked decorative
FIXED: shared/system.css (touch targets)
  — Keyboard and pointer operability: controls must be large enough to press (the site's own rule: 44px on touch)
  — On touch screens the streaming, YouTube and email buttons, the full-screen player's controls, the per-track lyrics buttons, the lyric lines and the skip link grow from 40px to 44px; mouse screens are unchanged
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (settings switches in the menu)
  — Screen reader semantics + pattern documentation: a control's name and its description are separate things
  — Each switch is now announced as "Effects, switch, on" with its explanation as the description, instead of one run-together name ("Single-key shortcutsG then a letter…"); the switch and fold patterns are documented in the component's comments
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (menu dialog, initial focus)
  — Keyboard operability: focus order must be safe and predictable; pattern documented in the component
  — Opening the menu by keyboard now puts focus on the first section button (or first setting on wide screens) instead of the "Listen on Apple Music" link, where a second press of Enter would have left the site
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (setting descriptions)
  — Accessible content: instructions in plain, complete sentences
  — "G then a letter to jump to a section, / to search" is now "Press G, then the first letter of a section, to jump to it. Press / to search."; "Xylophone notes when you press" is now "Plays a short note when you press a button"
FIXED: index-src.html (mini player's main button)
  — Meaningful contextual text: an aria-label replaces the button's visible words, so it must carry their meaning
  — The button is now announced as "Open full-screen player. Playing: <song>, from <album>" and updates with each song, instead of only "Open full-screen player"
FIXED: index-src.html (play button over each album cover)
  — Keyboard operability + meaningful names: a control must do from the keyboard what it shows, and be named for it
  — The cover button showed a play icon but was named "Show tracks for <album>" and opened the tracklist from the keyboard; it is now "Play <album>" / "Pause <album>" and plays or pauses with Enter or Space (mouse and touch unchanged; the pattern is documented in the code)
FIXED: index-src.html, scripts/prerender.py (tracklist buttons)
  — Meaningful contextual text: names must make sense out of context and include the visible label
  — The three "10 tracks" / "9 tracks" / "16 tracks" buttons are now announced with their album ("10 tracks on My Anima"), in both the pre-built page and the live-rendered cards
FIXED: shared/kinetic.js (links that open a new tab)
  — Meaningful contextual text: warn before a change of context
  — All 19 streaming and YouTube links (toolbar, cards, menu, both players, video viewer) now say "(opens in a new tab)" in their spoken name; the pattern is documented in the code and applies to links added later
FIXED: index-src.html (featured release buttons)
  — Meaningful contextual text: two links with the same name must go to the same place
  — "Listen on Apple Music" appeared twice with different destinations (artist page in the toolbar, the album on the first screen); the first-screen buttons now add the release name ("Listen on Apple Music: Ash Stu, Vol. II"), so no two controls on the page share a name
FIXED: scripts/build_lyrics_pages.py (skip link on the 34 lyric pages)
  — Keyboard operability: a skip link must move keyboard focus, not just scroll
  — On lyric pages the skip link scrolled but left focus on itself, so it skipped nothing; it now moves focus and goes straight to the song ("Skip to the song"), and toolbar section links move focus to their section too
FIXED: index-src.html (spoken announcements)
  — Screen reader announcements: use polite live regions for routine updates, assertive only for errors
  — A song change no longer interrupts the screen reader mid-sentence and is spoken once, not two to four times; error messages still interrupt. The pattern is documented beside the regions
FIXED: shared/system.css (high-contrast / forced-colours mode)
  — Visual clarity and system preferences: controls must stay visible when the system replaces the page's colours
  — In Windows Contrast Themes the menu button, Next, Close and most full-screen player icons were blank, the seek and volume tracks invisible and the current lyric unmarked; icons now take the system text colour, tracks are outlined and filled with the highlight colour, and the current lyric is outlined
FIXED: index-src.html, shared/system.css (song pages)
  — Screen reader access to primary content: content hidden for visual tidiness must stay available to assistive technology
  — On each of the 34 song pages the lyrics under the song's heading were removed entirely once the interactive copy opened; they are now only visually hidden, so a screen-reader user hears the words directly after "Skip to the song" and the title
